Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific BBB Rev D HDMI fix: debounce HPD disconnect glitch]

The IT66122 briefly drops the TV HPD signal during HDMI link re-negotiation
approximately 7 seconds into boot.  The IRQ handler reads HPD at the instant of
the interrupt and sees "disconnected".  drm_bridge_hpd_notify() propagates this
to drm_bridge_connector_hpd_cb(), which compares old_status (connected) with
new_status (disconnected), detects a change, and fires
drm_kms_helper_connector_hotplug_event() -> drm_fb_helper_restore_fbdev_mode_unlocked()
-> CRTC reprogram.  The TV briefly loses sync and re-applies its overscan
calibration, visible as a sudden zoom-in on screen.

Since it66121_irq_threaded_handler() runs in a kernel thread (IRQF_ONESHOT),
sleeping is allowed.  When a disconnect event is detected, sleep 200 ms and
re-read the actual HPD state.  The IT66122 reconnect completes within ~50-100 ms,
so the re-read returns "connected".  drm_bridge_connector_hpd_cb() then sees
old_status == new_status and returns early, suppressing the re-modeset and zoom.

For a genuine cable-unplug, HPD remains low after 200 ms and the disconnect is
correctly forwarded to the DRM framework.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
@@ -975,8 +975,18 @@ unlock:
 unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&ctx->lock);
 
-	if (event)
-		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(&ctx->bridge, status);
+	if (event) {
+		if (status == connector_status_disconnected) {
+			/* Debounce transient HPD disconnect from IT66122 HDMI re-negotiation at boot. */
+			msleep(200);
+			mutex_lock(&ctx->lock);
+			status = it66121_is_hpd_detect(ctx) ?
+				connector_status_connected :
+				connector_status_disconnected;
+			mutex_unlock(&ctx->lock);
+		}
+		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(&ctx->bridge, status);
+	}
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
